# Part 08: State of the art methods for reproducing a target height map with a layered Copernicus graph (11 October 2026)

Scope: this part collects the published methods, statistics, metrics and official SideFX resources that can drive the reproduction, as close to identical as possible, of a target HEIGHT map (often an AI generated reference) by a procedural Copernicus graph in Houdini 22.0.368, built one layer at a time and re-evaluated after every layer, then turns them into at least sixteen distinct methods for choosing and building the next layer. (11 October 2026)

Conventions: `UNVERIFIED` marks a claim inferred or reasoned rather than read in a source; `PROPOSED` marks a threshold, procedure or wiring designed here for our use and still to be calibrated on real targets; node names in `code` are internal Copernicus names taken from the local Houdini 22.0.368 list `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-height/dataset/cop_nodes_h22.txt`. (11 October 2026)

Sources were read through the web on 11 October 2026; every entry gives its URL or paper reference, and every paragraph is a paraphrase, never a copy. (11 October 2026)

