- Caveat on AI generated references: their grids are often slightly irregular (wavy grout, unequal tiles), which caps gate B and C for a perfect lattice; the remedy is a method that represents the irregularity (per tile index mapping, traced grout, M07 and M08), never a lowered threshold (PROPOSED). (11 October 2026)
- Caveat on alignment: a global sub pixel shift between output and reference can be removed with `alignpixels` or by phase correlation before the deterministic gates, but local warping must not be applied, since it would hide geometry errors (PROPOSED). (11 October 2026)

