### 5.26 The three most promising methods (11 October 2026)

- M01 residual driven greedy pursuit: it is exactly the decision rule the task asks for, choosing the next layer by measured gain, one layer at a time, reverting what does not pay, and it hosts every other builder as a move. (11 October 2026)
- M06 distance field transfer function fitting, fed by the masks of M04 and the lattice of M05: it gives pixel level identity of the dominant relief (grout, bevel, lines) from one measured curve, in two or three nodes, without any search. (11 October 2026)
- M13 spectrum and histogram matched stochastic layers: it reaches statistical identity of the random part cheaply and is judged by distributions, which removes the regression to the mean trap that makes pixel metrics reject correct detail. (11 October 2026)

